usage_logs.csv
survey_responses.csv

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Generated by analyze_survey.py -- local research output, not source
analysis_output/

# Research paper draft -- kept local, not part of the app codebase
research_paper_draft.md

# Internal engineering field guide (lessons, constraints, past bugs) --
# deliberately kept out of the public repo, and purged from git history
# 2026-08-06 before the repo went public. Code comments still cite it by
# name; ARCHITECTURE.md is the public map, this is the private manual.
CLAUDE.md

# Slide deck for counselor/teacher outreach -- kept local, not part of the app codebase
presentation/

# Marketing/outreach working files (src taxonomy, email templates, launch copy,
# send logs) -- kept local for the same reason as presentation/
#
# marketing/infographics/ holds the FULL-RESOLUTION chart PNGs (~1.6MB, 2080px
# wide) that the /charts gallery is built from. They stay out of git for the
# reason brand/guide-*.png does: infra/build_site.py writes web-sized JPEGs
# into static/ and those ARE committed, so carrying both would put the same
# picture in the repo twice at ten times the weight. static/ is the archive.
#
# The consequence, which is the whole point of writing it down: a fresh clone
# CANNOT rebuild the gallery images. Three of the six have generator scripts in
# this folder; the other three were hand-patched from exports that have no
# source at all. If static/info-*.jpg is ever deleted, it is gone.
marketing/

# Agent tooling: skills, settings, worktrees. Local working aids, not part of
# the app -- same reasoning as CLAUDE.md, which is also deliberately untracked.
# Ignored rather than merely untracked because commits here are routinely
# staged with `git add -A`, which would sweep them back in silently.
.claude/

# Everything feeding the research paper stays local, same as the draft above:
# scope/limitations notes, paper structure outlines, and any future drafts.
# Ignored rather than merely untracked -- this repo's commits are routinely
# staged with `git add -A`, which would sweep an untracked file in silently.
SCOPE.md
RETURNING_STUDENT_PLAN.md
*_PLAN.md
paper_outline.md
paper_*.md
*_draft.md
Most-Recent-Cohorts-Institution.csv
