# Wrangler's local state (build cache, deploy metadata, login token pointer).
# Never contains the token itself -- that lives in ~/.wrangler -- but it is
# per-machine and has no business in the repo.
.wrangler/

# Guide imagery: build output in brand/, SERVED copy in static/. Only the
# served copy is committed -- the pair is byte-identical and 4.7MB, and
# carrying both means every regeneration writes the same bytes to git twice.
#
# Nothing is lost. The two diagrams rebuild from brand/build_guide_graphics.py
# with no credentials, and the AI heroes are not regenerable anyway (a rerun of
# build_ai_hero.py costs an API call and, for a changed prompt, returns a
# different photograph) -- so static/ is the archive, and `--cards-only` reads
# its social cards back out of static/ rather than out of brand/.
#
# The nine OLDER brand/*.png are already tracked and stay that way: an ignore
# rule does not untrack a tracked file, and quietly deleting published assets
# is not what "stop carrying duplicates" asked for.
brand/guide-*.png
# Same rule, same reason, for the calculator link-preview card. Its INPUT is
# the exception and IS committed: brand/sources/ holds a browser screenshot of
# the running app, which no script can regenerate, so it is source rather than
# output.
brand/feature-og-*.png

# Two generated files in static/ that nothing serves, kept on disk but out of
# git so they do not read as published assets:
#   guide-hero-1600x460.png              build_guide_graphics.build()'s
#                                        credential-free fallback hero. Every
#                                        post now names a real hero, so this is
#                                        only proof the repo builds with no
#                                        Cloudflare credentials present.
#   guide-hero-for-parents-run-the-numbers.png
#                                        the pre-AI flat-navy hero for that
#                                        post, superseded by the -klein4b one.
#                                        Committing it would put TWO heroes in
#                                        static/ for one slug, which is exactly
#                                        what broke build_ai_hero --cards-only
#                                        when it globbed instead of reading
#                                        front matter.
static/guide-hero-1600x460.png
static/guide-hero-for-parents-run-the-numbers.png
